=== RUN   TestDiagAnchoredChips

=== does anchoring the chips on the calendar beat placing them by week?
Every arm plays the SAME chips: bench boost, free hit, triple captain.
NO ARM PLAYS A WILDCARD. Holding it at a common week made the
full-sight arm the only one boosting a wildcard-rebuilt squad — 30 of
30 cells against 3-5 for the lag arms — which is a bigger confound
than the GW4 one it was removing. Every arm now boosts a squad built
for something else, so that floor cancels.
What varies is placement: the control uses fixed offsets from entry,
which is what every earlier chip measurement here used, and the
anchored arms read the fixture calendar.
**The full-sight arm is a target, not a policy**: FPL announces
doubles as cup rounds resolve. The lag arms are what a manager runs,
and they will not spend a chip on a week involving fewer than 4 clubs.
**Read points per season-path, not per gameweek.** Three chips are an
event count, and dividing a one-off by weeks played inflates the late
entries — see the harness-and-inference note.

